I've added Dockerfile, .dockerignore and fly.toml at the repo root. I haven't
  committed them, and I haven't built them: there's no Docker or flyctl on this machine,
  so the first fly deploy is the real test. It builds the web app, then acctd with the  
  web app embedded, and runs it with the database on a /data volume.

  Run these from the repo root in PowerShell:

  # 1. Install the Fly CLI and log in (creates or uses your Fly account; it asks for a  
  card)
  iwr https://fly.io/install.ps1 -useb | iex
  fly auth login

  # 2. Create the app. The name must be globally unique, so change acct-test
  #    here and in fly.toml if it's taken.
  fly apps create acct-test

  # 3. Create the 1 GB volume for the SQLite file, in Sydney (the closest Fly region to 
  NZ)
  fly volumes create acct_data --region syd --size 1 -a acct-test

  # 4. Build and deploy. --ha=false keeps it to one machine, which SQLite needs.        
  fly deploy --ha=false

  The first deploy compiles Rust on Fly's builder, so expect 10 to 20 minutes. Once it  
  succeeds, create your user by opening a shell on the machine and running init:        

  fly ssh console -a acct-test
  # then, inside the machine:
  acctd init

  acctd init asks for the practice name, username, full name and password. The password 
  must be at least 10 characters. After that, open https://acct-test.fly.dev and log in.
  If init complains about the terminal, tell me the error. It asks for the password     
  with rpassword, which needs a real terminal.

  To point your own domain at it:
  1. Run fly certs add yourdomain.com -a acct-test.
  2. Add the DNS records it prints, either at Vercel's DNS or wherever the domain is.   

  What to know before sharing the link
  - No login throttling yet. Throttling and two-factor sign-in are M12. Use a strong    
    password and don't post the URL publicly.
  - Session cookie lacks the Secure flag. It is HttpOnly and SameSite=Strict, and       
    force_https means it only travels over HTTPS in practice. Setting Secure properly is
    an M12 job. I can add an env-var switch for it now if you want.
  - Machine stops when idle. I set auto_stop_machines, so the first request after a     
    quiet spell takes a few seconds. To keep it always on, set min_machines_running = 1,
    which costs a little more.
  - No backups yet. The volume is a single disk, so treat it as disposable test data.   
    fly volumes snapshots list -a acct-test shows Fly's automatic daily snapshots.      
  - Repo noise. The packages/types files showing as modified in git status are unrelated
    to this. Please check what a commit of the whole tree would include before using    
    zz_quicksave.txt.

  If the build fails, paste me the error.

